.TH TULPAR-STATS 1 "2026" "tulpar 0.7.0" "Tulpar Manual"
.SH NAME
tulpar-stats \- show package database statistics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tulpar stats
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B tulpar t
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B tulpar \-t
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Summarises the package database: the number of installed packages,
how many were installed explicitly or as dependencies, how many are
held, how many are orphans, and the total number of recorded files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dest " " \fIpath\fR
Operate on the database of an alternate root.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Print the counters as a JSON object instead of human-readable text. See
.BR tulpar-json (7).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if the database cannot be read.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tulpar (1),
.BR tulpar-list (1),
.BR tulpar-orphans (1),
.BR tulpar-json (7)
